---
// The home page intro, shown as a card in the right sidebar (pages with `intro: true`).
// Neutral structure; pink and green only where they mean something (see /design).
// One tile per example on the home page, linking to its section. The pink dot marks a problem.
const examples = [
	['Quint', 'late reply', '#can-a-slow-response-overwrite-newer-search-results'],
	['TLA+', 'stuck cache key', '#can-one-failed-database-call-break-a-cache-key-for-good'],
	['Lean', 'negative price', '#can-this-discount-make-the-price-negative'],
	['Dafny', 'missed id', '#does-this-binary-search-find-every-id'],
];
---

<div class="home-intro">
	<p class="eyebrow">Formal methods for TypeScript</p>
	<p class="story"><strong>A module of an ordinary TS codebase can go sideways.</strong> We feel comfortable with 95% of the code, but not this one piece. Scary to change, impossible to describe, and painful to test.</p>
	<p class="story"><strong>Formal methods are first of all a thinking tool.</strong> They make the system easier to understand, and where they don't, at least safe to change and maintain. Correctness comes after.</p>
	<p class="story"><strong>The TS ecosystem falls short, but the industry has a lot to offer.</strong> TLA+, Quint, Lean, Dafny and more. Here we will try to bridge the gap and show how to use a wide selection of tools in a TypeScript project.</p>
	<p class="story"><strong>They used to require special skills, not anymore.</strong> AI coding agents close that gap for professional software engineers.</p>
	<div class="examples">
		<p class="examples-title">Worked examples</p>
		<ul>
			{
				examples.map(([tool, problem, href]) => (
					<li>
						<a href={href}>
							<b>{tool}</b>
							<span>{problem}</span>
						</a>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.home-intro {
		/* The fixed right sidebar is wider than its visible column, so size the card to that column: Starlight makes it
		   the sidebar width plus half the space left beside the content. */
		box-sizing: border-box;
		max-width: min(
			18.5rem,
			calc(
				var(--sl-sidebar-width) + (100vw - 2 * var(--sl-sidebar-width) - var(--sl-content-width)) / 2 - 2 *
					var(--sl-sidebar-pad-x) - 0.5rem
			)
		);
		margin: 1rem var(--sl-sidebar-pad-x);
		padding: 1.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sc-border);
		border-radius: 1rem;
		background: var(--sc-surface);
		color: var(--sc-text);
	}
	.home-intro p {
		margin: 0;
	}
	.eyebrow {
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--sc-muted);
	}
	.story {
		margin-top: 0.75rem !important;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--sc-muted);
	}
	.story strong {
		display: block;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--sc-text);
	}

	/* Links to the examples below. */
	.examples {
		margin-top: 1.25rem;
		padding-top: 1rem;
		border-top: 1px dashed var(--sc-border);
	}
	.examples-title {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.examples ul {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0.65rem 0 0;
		padding: 0;
	}
	.examples a {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.1rem;
		padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sc-border);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		background: var(--sc-bg);
		color: var(--sc-text);
		text-decoration: none;
		line-height: 1.25;
		transition: border-color 0.15s;
	}
	.examples a:hover,
	.examples a:focus-visible {
		border-color: var(--sc-text);
	}
	.examples b {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
	}
	.examples a span {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		white-space: nowrap;
		color: var(--sc-muted);
	}
	.examples a span::before {
		content: '';
		width: 0.4rem;
		height: 0.4rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--sc-pink);
		flex: none;
	}

	@media (max-width: 71.99rem) {
		.home-intro {
			max-width: none;
			margin: 0.75rem var(--sl-content-pad-x) 0;
		}
		.examples ul {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
